{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1134969-using-masques-as-dirges-and-masks","id":1134969,"title":"Using Masques as Dirges and Masks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T15:21:07-07:00","id":1134969,"title":"Using Masques as Dirges and Masks","content":"Thought occurred to me today that the Masques featured in the Mage Guardian Order book are suppose to be essential character archetypes, according to the Guardians. Each Masque is a Virtue/Vice pair using the old fixed seven of each. So hope, faith, prudence, etc for virtue, and pride, lust, sloth, etc for vice.<br /> <br /> Well...wouldn't they work as niffy masks and dirges? They just need a bit of a name rework as some names are far too arcane sounding. 'Apprentice Forge-Coal' is a cool name but it sticks out when placed beside 'child' and 'deviant'. Some are fine: 'whip' and 'factor' have that quick, punchy vibe. They also need clear examples of willpower regain but I assume the original bios, the virtue/vice pairing, and a little imagination is solution enough for that. Still, be fun to see what people come up with.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thought I'd share. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  forgot clear examples 08-28-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Pos